//! What a session with the Launchpad CLI tool (`vault::LAUNCHPAD_TOOL`) is told about it.

/// What a session granted the Launchpad CLI tool (`vault::LAUNCHPAD_TOOL`) is told: read Launchpad state and
/// write proposals. `workspace`: the session's workspace, the default scope of the list commands.
pub fn cli_reference(cli: &str, workspace: Option<&str>, access: crate::vault::LaunchpadAccess) -> String {
    use crate::vault::LaunchpadAccess;
    let ws_arg = workspace.map(|id| format!(" --workspace {id}")).unwrap_or_default();
    let routine_triggers = crate::routines::TRIGGER_FORMS;
    let ready_actions: Vec<&crate::actions::Action> = crate::actions::ACTIONS.iter().filter(|a| a.ready).collect();
    let ready = ready_actions.iter().map(|a| a.name).collect::<Vec<_>>().join("|");
    let ready_lines: String = ready_actions.iter().map(|a| format!("  - `{}`: {} (args: {}; input: {})\n", a.name, a.help, crate::actions::params(a).join(", "), if a.input.is_empty() { "none".into() } else { a.input.iter().map(|f| if f.optional { format!("{}?", f.name) } else { f.name.to_string() }).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(", ") })).collect();
    let level = match access { LaunchpadAccess::Read => "read", LaunchpadAccess::Propose => "propose", LaunchpadAccess::Admin => "admin" };
    let mut out = format!(
        "# Launchpad CLI\n\nYour access to the owner's Launchpad through `{cli}` (JSON output) is **{level}** (set by the owner: `launchpad` in a bot's bot.toml). Through the CLI you never post to GitHub, send messages to other people, read credentials or enable paid usage.\n\n\
Read (add `--workspace <id or name>` for another workspace):\n\
- `{cli} folders list{ws_arg}`\n- `{cli} bots list{ws_arg}` (bots: persistent agents with one thread each, their job and current session)\n- `{cli} sessions list{ws_arg}` and `{cli} sessions show <session-id>`\n- `{cli} profiles list` (profiles and the quota of each subscription login)\n- `{cli} presets list` (only presets with agent=true belong in proposed launch specs)\n- `{cli} inbox list{ws_arg}` (thread ids; a bot whose bot.toml says `inbox_done = true` marks them done with `{cli} inbox done <id>...`, others propose an `inbox.done` ready card)\n- `{cli} schedules list{ws_arg}`\n- `{cli} proposals list{ws_arg}` (proposal ids, titles, states and contents)\n- `{cli} today{ws_arg}` (what waits for the owner: questions, finished agents, cards, drafts to send, GitHub items, failed routines)\n- `{cli} activity list{ws_arg}` (what sessions with admin access changed directly, with the values before)\n- `{cli} trace <session-id>` for an agent's full trace (redirect it to a file)\n"
    );
    if access >= LaunchpadAccess::Propose {
        out.push_str(&format!(
            "\n\nProposals are inert cards: the owner starts them with a click (a bot in auto mode starts one-time launches, messages and schedules at once). Propose with `{cli} propose <launch|message|schedule|cron|status|preset|tool|bot|routine|bot-instructions|ready|report> --title \"…\" [--note \"…\"] [--replaces <proposal-id>] --spec-file <file.json>`. The JSON file holds:\n\
- launch: {{\"spec\": <launch spec>}}\n- message: {{\"session_id\": \"…\", \"text\": \"…\"}} (to steer an agent that already works on it)\n- schedule: {{\"spec\": <launch spec>, \"conditions\": [{{\"kind\": \"in\", \"minutes\": 30}} | {{\"kind\": \"at\", \"at\": <unix ms>}} | {{\"kind\": \"agents\", \"session_ids\": [\"…\"]}} | {{\"kind\": \"quota\", \"harness\": \"claude\", \"window\": \"five_hour\"}}]}}\n- cron: {{\"spec\": <launch spec>, \"schedule\": \"0 9 * * 1\", \"conditions\": []}}\n- status: {{\"session_ids\": [\"…\"]}} (a list of sessions to look at)\n- preset: {{\"label\": \"…\", \"text\": \"<sentence added to prompts>\", \"agent\": true}} creates a preset; add \"preset_id\": \"<id from presets list>\" to update that preset instead (give its full new label, text and agent flag). Presets cannot be deleted through proposals.\n- tool: {{\"tool\": {{\"id\": \"example\", \"name\": \"Example CLI\", \"install\": {{\"kind\": \"github_release\" | \"url\" | \"cargo\" | \"uv\" | \"npm\", \"source\": \"…\", \"asset\": \"…\"}} or null, \"credential\": \"example\", \"env\": [\"EXAMPLE_TOKEN\"], \"hosts\": [{{\"host\": \"api.example.com\", \"auth\": {{\"kind\": \"bearer\"}}}}], \"workspaces\": [\"*\"], \"check_url\": \"https://api.example.com/me\", \"vars\": {{\"EXAMPLE_FORMAT\": \"json\"}} (settings that are not secret, set only when its commands run; needs an install)}}, \"token_url\": \"https://…\"}} adds a tool to Home's registry; the owner then pastes its token.\n- bot: {{\"name\": \"Scout\", \"instructions\": \"# Scout\\n\\n<its job and how the owner likes it done>\", \"profile\": \"<profile id>\", \"folder\": \"<folder id>\" or null}} creates a bot in this workspace; it starts nothing. Without a folder (the usual choice), each session starts in a temporary folder and adds worktrees of the folders a task needs; set a folder only for a bot that always works on one.\n- routine: {{\"bot_id\": \"<bot id>\", \"title\": \"Daily check\", \"instructions\": \"<what the bot does at each run>\", \"trigger\": {routine_triggers}, \"schedule\": \"30 8 * * 1-5\" (schedule trigger only), \"conditions\": []}} adds a routine to a bot of this workspace: its runs are messages to the bot's thread, ending with a report or `no_update`.\n- report: {{\"outcome\": \"needs_you\" | \"merged\" | \"approved\" | \"commented\" | \"waiting\" | \"closed\" | \"info\", \"github\": \"owner/repo#123\" (optional), \"body\": \"<Markdown: what you did and why, or your question and the exact text you would post>\"}} tells the owner what you did about one item, one card per item (title: the item and the outcome in a few words). `needs_you` waits as a question; the owner's reply comes to your thread naming the card. A new report about the same GitHub item replaces your waiting one.\n- bot-instructions: {{\"bot_id\": \"<bot id>\", \"instructions\": \"<the whole new BOT.md>\"}} proposes a new BOT.md for a bot of this workspace (your own included); the owner sees the diff.\n- ready: {{\"action\": \"<{ready}>\", \"args\": [<route ids>], \"input\": {{<body fields>}}, \"session_id\": \"<the session it is about; required for worktree.merge>\"}} prepares a click that stays the owner's (merge, publish, post, send, run CI, mark Inbox threads done, update Home): the card runs the same call as the button on its page, with the same confirmation, and only on the owner's click. Routes and fields:\n{ready_lines}\n\
A launch spec is {{\"text\": \"<prompt>\", \"profile\": \"<profile id>\", \"target\": {{\"kind\": \"project\", \"project_id\": \"<folder id>\"}} or {{\"kind\": \"temp\"}} (a temporary folder, deleted when the agent is archived), \"worktree\": {{\"base\": null, \"include_changes\": false, \"when_done\": \"keep\"}} for Git folders (`when_done` is \"keep\", \"merge\", \"local_pr\" or \"read_only\" for questions and audits that change nothing), \"github_refs\": [], \"presets\": [<preset ids>]}}; other fields take their defaults. Launchpad validates each proposal like the composer's preview and refuses invalid ones: read the error and fix the file. One proposal per independent task. To refine a card that still waits, find it with `proposals list` and use `--replaces <proposal-id>` (only proposed or failed cards of the same workspace), and say which card you replaced. After proposing, check the returned state.\n"
        ));
    }
    if access == LaunchpadAccess::Admin {
        use crate::actions::{ACTIONS, ActionAccess, usage};
        out.push_str(&format!(
            "\n\n## Admin\n\nYou may also run these actions directly; each one is the same API call as the owner's button (`{cli} do <action> …` works too). Positional arguments are the ids from the list commands; `--body-file` takes a JSON file. Act directly only when the owner asked for that change or your instructions say so; otherwise propose. Say what you changed, and read it back to check.\n\n"
        ));
        for a in ACTIONS.iter().filter(|a| a.access == ActionAccess::Admin) {
            let body = a.body_file.map(|b| format!(" (body: {b})")).unwrap_or_default();
            out.push_str(&format!("- `{}`: {}{body}\n", usage(cli, a), a.help));
        }
        let owner: Vec<&str> = ACTIONS.iter().filter(|a| a.access == ActionAccess::Owner).map(|a| a.help).collect();
        out.push_str(&format!(
            "\nEach direct change goes to the owner's activity list, with Undo when the action has one (`{cli} activity list`). A Home update restarts Home a few minutes after your call returns: your session keeps running on its runner, and Launchpad CLI calls that need Home fail until it is back; then run `{cli} home check-update` to see what it runs. Only the owner's click runs these, never you: {}. Propose a ready card for merge, publish, post, send, run CI and Inbox done, and a tool card for tools. Every other change (profiles, the rest of config.toml, the Outbox, channels, credentials, devices, terminals, runners, Burst, setup fixes, folder setup commands, paid usage) is refused: ask the owner. `{cli} api <GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE> <path> [--body-file <file.json>]` reads any other state (GET) and runs the same actions by their API path.",
            owner.iter().map(|h| h[..1].to_lowercase() + &h[1..]).collect::<Vec<_>>().join("; ")
        ));
        out.push_str(&format!(
            "\n\n## Diagnose Launchpad\n\nYou may read Launchpad's own state to find out why something failed (no secret is ever shown: tokens and credentials are redacted or left out):\n\
- `{cli} health`: everything failing now, by area (sessions, runners, Burst, routines, schedules, cards, quota, harnesses, MCP, channels, GitHub, backups, Home update, setup), with the ids to look at. Start here.\n\
- `{cli} logs [--session <id>] [--runner <id or name> | --home | --local] [--since 2h] [--level warn] [--grep <text>] [--json]`: recent log lines of Home and every connected runner, oldest first; `--session` keeps the lines about a session and its Burst runners. The real reason of a failure is usually here.\n\
- `{cli} sessions show <id>`: a session with its runner, generation, launch spec, last error (`failure`), Burst runs and latest handoff.\n\
- `{cli} failures [--since 1d]`: what Home noticed failing (sessions, Burst jobs, routine runs, scheduled launches, runners offline with work, Home restarts).\n\
- `{cli} runners list`, `{cli} burst runs [--session <id>]`, `{cli} burst job <runner id>` (the HF Job's stage and log), `{cli} home` (uptime, starts and whether each stopped cleanly, backups, update), `{cli} tools list` (tools, credential names, MCP servers and their errors), `{cli} channels list`.\n\
A routine with the trigger {{\"kind\": \"failure\", \"events\": [\"any\"]}} tells you about new failures without polling. Diagnose, then report what failed and why, with the fix you propose; act on Launchpad records only as your instructions allow.\n"
        ));
    }
    out
}
